patient that includes:
1434 (a) identification of [all services and products] a service or a product provided to the patient by the
hearing instrument specialist and the charges for each service or product;
1437 (b) a statement whether [any] a hearing instrument provided to a patient is "new," "used," or
"reconditioned" and the terms and conditions of any warranty or guarantee that applies to each
instrument; and
1440 (c) the identity and license number of each hearing instrument specialist or hearing instrument intern
who provided services or products to the patient;
1442 (4) before providing services or products to a patient:
1443 (a) advise the patient regarding services and products offered to the patient, including the expected
results of the services and products;
- 44 -

